33	// HIP gfx942 launch glue for Prodigy.
34	// Algorithm: csrc/algorithms/prodigy.h
35	//
36	// COMPUTE PATTERN
37	// Mixed: per-element + reduction.
38	//   Per element: r_local += g * (p_init - p) * d²
39	//                s_local += d² * |g|
40	//                AdamW apply with d as the lr scale
41	//   Reduction:   r_global = sum(r_local) across all elements (single FP32 scalar)
42	//                s_global = sum(s_local) across all elements
43	//                d_new = max(d_prev, r_global / |s_global|)
44	// The reduction is the bottleneck: needs wavefront reduce → LDS tree reduce
45	// → cross-block (cooperative or atomic) final reduce.
46	//
47	// MFMA APPLICABILITY: none.
48	// The reduction needs wave-reduce (DPP on CDNA3), then LDS-tree across waves
49	// in a block, then a single AGENT-scope atomic to a global counter. No GEMM,
50	// no MFMA. The §5 AMDGCN kernel implements exactly this 2-level tree.
51	//
52	// WHY ATEN HERE (for the apply)
53	// ATen's `.sum()` dispatches to rocPRIM's segmented reduction, which on
54	// MI300X already uses wave-reduce + LDS-tree internally; the §5 kernel
55	// hand-writes the r/s reduction with the DPP→LDS→AGENT-atomic tree (the
56	// high-value AMDGCN piece). The AdamW apply stays on the ATen host path.
